WEBVTT

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.730
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.030
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.740
but also in crime.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.990
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.660
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.580
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.230
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.030
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.030
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.410
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.420
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.250
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:18.470
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:25.060
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.400
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:37.200
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.740
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.420
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.390
Christmas eve.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.270
Kanuka's grandmother,
visiting from Hawaii, is missing.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.980
The only clue was her message,
"The Christmas of fifty years ago."

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.270
At the same time, a mysterious
tanker entered Tokyo Bay.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.070
Its goal: Field testing a new anti-
Labor electromagnetic weapon.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.530
Division 1 was lured to Teleport
City, then all contact was lost.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.160
Although Kanuka was worried
about her grandmother,

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.040
she returned to duty.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.710
Now, she and Ota
are in serious trouble.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.000
Eve's Shudder

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:54.980
Kanuka!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.240
- Why, you!
- Calm down!

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.080
Asuma!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.160
- Hey!
- Get back!

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.170
This isn't like a
construction Labor.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.790
Get out, even if you
have to sacrifice an arm!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.170
I can't do that!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.300
Don't underestimate
Alphonse!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.430
Take this!

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.110
Noa, here comes
another one!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.370
Asuma, don't I deserve
a little praise for that?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.120
- A little.
- Meanie.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.830
You have to get back to
the captain and report.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:53.620
But...

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.090
I'm going to collect
Kanuka and Ota. Now go!

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.220
One Brocken is
out of commission.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.930
A second is damaged,
but operable.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.760
Instruct the Phantom
to change targets.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.680
Who are you?

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.650
Ota, you can't
beat him alone!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.520
Ota!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.610
Get in, Kanuka!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.570
But Ota...
I'm responsible...

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.280
Calm down, Kanuka!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.950
He's behind armor.
He's fine. Now get in!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.750
Shinohara,
where's Izumi?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.010
- She retreated!
- What?

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.420
This is no time to run away!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.720
I thought you could
adapt to circumstances!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:49.760
You won't escape!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.140
YOU'RE the one being chased,
you know.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.770
- Ota!
- Behind you!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.110
- Ota!
- I'm fine!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.990
I don't care if I
lose a monitor or two!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.080
Ota, stop!
You're no match for him!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.880
Now it's payback time!

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.060
What are you up to now?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.520
Oh, no! I can't move!
I can't move!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.530
System error?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.650
It's an electromagnetic pulse!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.370
- Get out, Ota!
- But...

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.620
If your Ingram can't move,
it's no good! Follow orders!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.710
Doesn't this thing
have a self-destruct?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.000
Why would we need one?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:10.800
Ota!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.260
What are you doing, Noa?
Do you think they just got lucky?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.310
Go on!
Get out of here!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.350
Asuma!

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.560
What?

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.230
Be careful.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.860
What was that all about?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.130
You idiot!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.550
Ota!

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.890
Take this!

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.770
His movement disk!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.810
Avenge me!
Swear you'll avenge me!

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.570
Kanuka, we'll be back.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.790
- Let's go.
- Okay.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.080
They're here!
Who's there?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.340
- Are you with Special Vehicles?
- What if I am?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.420
We'll handle this now.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.350
A Helldiver?
The Ground Defense Force!

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.270
Don't let your captain
know that we're here.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.230
Keep it a secret?

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.190
Just continue with
your mission.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.190
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.650
The enemy's using
an electron beam.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.650
It's very powerful.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.620
Roger. Are you
with Division 1?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.080
No, I'm Noa Izumi of
Division 2. Good luck.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.830
You too, Officer Izumi.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.340
Two defense Labors approaching.
Shinohara assaults, model 99.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.180
Nothing to worry about...
It's just a bigger sample.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.680
Bring the Phantom
around to deal with them.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.980
Shouldn't we be going, too?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.520
- To do what?
- To do what?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.310
Look...
they're coming back.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.700
- Hiromi!
- Yes?

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:26.120
Charge the batteries and
fix the left patrol light.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:27.960
Officer Izumi...

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:35.550
Grab on!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.470
Asuma!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:49.560
Tears?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.730
That's strange.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.840
You can't get away with
kicking a police officer!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.800
You're okay!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.300
You don't look
so okay yourself.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.010
Where are Ota, Nagumo,
and the others?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.220
I'm sure they're fine.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:30.480
I think our opponents
missed their target.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.110
- Missed?
- They haven't got it.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.320
Captain, what about Shinshi?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.400
I haven't heard from him.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:49.290
The base is a big place to search.
What if our guess is wrong?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.460
It's big, but it has its limits.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.750
Maybe we'll stumble
across something.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:57.210
Yes?

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:07.140
We have to gather intelligence.
Advance when ready.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:07.810
Roger.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:15.480
After it!

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.780
Four Brockens and
an unknown Labor.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.290
They aren't here on their own...
Their commander must be nearby.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.710
Find him.
Avoid combat, if possible.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.710
Roger!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.210
It's cold out.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:45.850
Selkie H-10

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.850
Kutei Labor

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.680
- Here I go!
- It's a trap!

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.270
It's them!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.480
Wait, Noa!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.110
She can't do it alone.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.400
Ota's machine
might still work.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:44.700
Hang on, Noa.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.540
Mrs. Rei Clancy?

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:59.250
Yes, that's what I've been
telling this man.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:02.800
Report back on the radio.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.720
You found her? Roger.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.220
But how do I
let them know?

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.650
They know we're on to them,

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:23.150
and the EM jamming will
prevent a helicopter pick-up.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.530
Captain, permission
to open fire?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.990
Denied. We can't leave
any trace of gunpowder.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.580
- I'll buy you some time.
- But...

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.250
You can't hide your
presence much longer.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.210
There's an unknown Labor
back at the construction site.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.760
Listen up: On our way out,
we'll eliminate the Brocken.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:48.430
Roger.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.530
We can't stay long.
Retreat.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.410
We'll meet again.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.640
I'm missing something.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.930
Captain, look!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:38.390
Follow it.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.730
Labor carrier
following at 4 o'clock.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:49.820
They finally found us.
Signal everyone to withdraw.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:54.160
Abandon the damaged Brocken.
Cover the Phantom's retreat.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.420
Why, you!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:12.510
No effect!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.140
That same trick
won't work on me!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.360
Asuma?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:37.490
Now!

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.670
They found her!
They found Kanuka's grandmother!

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.890
December 24, 1950.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.140
We were at a Christmas party
when he was called to duty.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:02.440
The Chinese army had
crossed the 38th parallel,

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.560
and they were moving
to capture a fort.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:10.740
Later, the UN called this
"the retreat of December."

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:16.660
My husband
never came back.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:26.710
You have to work!

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.800
It's all right.
It can still move.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:39.510
Don't push it.
We don't know how damaged it is.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.440
It's sweet of you to say that,
but save your worries for her.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.740
I have to find out
what's going on outside.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.870
The guards are acting strange.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.570
The guards are gone.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.370
I can't see! Asuma!

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:52.250
I couldn't believe
he was dead.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:58.220
I thought if I waited just a little
longer, he'd come flying back.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.390
It still feels that way.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:08.600
It was over 40 years
before I could accept things.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:15.070
So can you see how I felt
when Kanuka joined the police?

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:22.080
I came to Japan to
bring her back home.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:29.920
People are so noble in the name
of their country, or justice.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:34.300
I'd trade away all that virtue,
just to keep my family safe.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.510
Would you?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:42.890
I chose this line of work
purely for my own sake.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.520
I think Kanuka may be the same.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:51.730
I fight, not for virtue and
nobility, but for myself.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.110
Noa, abandon your machine!

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:04.120
No! I've come too far
to give up now!

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:22.590
Kanuka! They found
your grandmother!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.550
The electromagnetic baton!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.320
The Phantom's laser
cannon is off-line.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:43.910
Where's the
field-test data?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.030
Right here.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.540
Withdraw the Phantom.
It's time for us to vanish, as well.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.930
- What?
- Be careful.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.430
Captain!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:12.940
Not bad.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.110
Kanuka!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.700
How dare you!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:28.910
Noa!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:41.840
We did it!

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.640
It self-destructed?

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.330
It looks like
you drove them back.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:22.050
No, we lost. We didn't
catch any of them.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.010
At least we destroyed
their mystery Labor!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:29.600
Did we? I suspect
that was another ruse.

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:33.470
But Izumi sure did
some fine work today!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.330
Why aren't you seeing
your grandmother off?

00:21:55.370 --> 00:22:00.170
She came to Japan just because
she was worried about you.

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:00.710
Shut up!

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.170
Mind your own business.

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:30.990
Is that what I looked like,
as you flew off, dear?

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:45.880
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:49.590
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:55.850
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:05.360
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:08.280
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:12.870
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:17.540
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:20.370
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:24.540
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:31.050
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.310
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:38.850
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:42.060
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:46.150
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:52.320
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:58.370
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:05.000
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.210
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.210
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:17.350
Is it a freak of nature
or a divine intervention?

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.270
Ota, the resident wallflower
of Division 2,

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:21.640
goes on a preliminary date
of an arranged marriage!!

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:25.730
This bizarre turn of events creates
quite a stir among Ota's colleagues.

00:24:25.940 --> 00:24:28.270
So Ota-san, would you
give us a comment?

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:30.490
You know a nice restaurant
with a view?

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:33.030
Dear o dear, will there be a
bright future for your love life?

00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:37.370
Next time, "Ota's Afternoon of
Puzzlement" Target locked on!

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:41.620
Next episode

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:41.620
Ota's Afternoon of Puzzlement
